# 1Password CLI template - no real values here, only secret references.
# Create a 1Password item named "Pluk-signing" in the "DesgnSpace" vault
# with the fields listed below. The field names must match exactly — the left-hand
# side here is the reference, the right-hand annotation is the field name.
#
# Required 1Password field setup (item: "Pluk-signing"):
#   APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY          - Developer ID Application certificate identity (e.g. "Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAMID)")
#   APPLE_ID                        - Apple ID email for notarization
#   APPLE_PASSWORD                  - app-specific password for that Apple ID
#   APPLE_TEAM_ID                   - Apple Developer Team ID (10-char, e.g. "A1B2C3D4E5")
#   TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY       - Minisign private key for updater (content of ~/.tauri/pluk.key)
#   TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD - password for the private key, if any (leave empty if none)
#
# If your vault is not "DesgnSpace", replace the vault name in the references below.
# See https://developer.1password.com/docs/cli/secrets-environment-variables/
#
# The Developer ID Application certificate (.p12) is not listed here — it is not
# an env var. It lives in a separate 1Password Document item, "Pluk Developer ID
# Certificate", in the same vault, and gets imported into the login keychain once.
# codesign then reads it by identity name (APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY, above), not
# from the environment. See docs/release-checklist.md, one-time setup.

APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY=op://DesgnSpace/Pluk-signing/APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY
APPLE_ID=op://DesgnSpace/Pluk-signing/APPLE_ID
APPLE_PASSWORD=op://DesgnSpace/Pluk-signing/APPLE_PASSWORD
APPLE_TEAM_ID=op://DesgnSpace/Pluk-signing/APPLE_TEAM_ID
TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=op://DesgnSpace/Pluk-signing/TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY
TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=op://DesgnSpace/Pluk-signing/TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD
